            },
            "privateNotes": "",
            "publicNotes": "<p>When stories of terminites first spread, they were viewed as eerie, furtive scavengers. When thrill-seekers began hunting the creatures for sport or study, a new type of terminite appeared almost overnight: the terminite hunter. Hunters are far more bloodthirsty than the smaller worker components of a terminite colony. Instead of harvesting motes from objects and terrain, hunters are strong enough to rip chunks of reality from living creatures.</p><hr /><h2>Infestations</h2><p>Invasive creatures plague Absalom Station and resist the most dedicated efforts to eliminate them. Whether lurking in the Ghost Levels or stowing away on starships, tenacious infestations are a constant problem in such a large and cosmopolitan station.</p>",
            "publication": {
                "license": "ORC",
                "remaster": true,
                "title": "Starfinder Absalom Station"
            }
